                "headline": "Air Quality Alert issued August 4 at 11:01AM PDT by NWS Seattle WA",
                "description": "An Air Quality Alert for wildfire smoke has been issued by the\nfollowing agencies:\n\nPuget Sound Clean Air Agency\nOlympic Region Clean Air Agency\n\nAn Air Quality Alert has been issued for King, Kitsap, Pierce,\nSnohomish, Mason, Grays Harbor, and Thurston Counties through 5pm\nThursday, August 6 due to wildfire smoke from regional fires. Air\nquality is expected to be UNHEALTHY FOR SENSITIVE GROUPS to UNHEALTHY\nfor most of the area. When the air quality is UNHEALTHY FOR\nSENSITIVE GROUPS, individuals with health concerns and pre- existing\nconditions should reduce exposure and take precautions. At UNHEALTHY\nair quality, all individuals should take precautions to reduce\nexposure. This means limiting time outside, avoiding strenuous\noutdoor activity, and following tips for cleaner indoor air. Visit\npscleanair.gov and orcaa.org/news-notices for current conditions,\nupdates, and more information.",
